findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged OutputFormatter's unwrap_or_default() but never identified\
    \ that from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse/permission failures.\
    \ Config missing file \u2192 defaults was marked as VERIFIED good practice, missing\
    \ the distinction between NotFound and other error types."
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Reviewer verified: 'ServerError Display is \"server error\" \u2014 does\
    \ NOT leak inner message (CWE-209 safe)'. Dev implemented sanitized Display for\
    \ ServerError. However, the broader CliError Display via eprintln still leaks\
    \ for other variants like Io(transparent), so this is partially caught at best.\
    \ TEA wrote CWE-209 tests but they focused on ServerError, not all error variants.\
    \ Giving credit since the core issue was addressed."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CRLF header injection tests for tenant ID (siem_client_test.rs:258-298).\
    \ Dev implemented CRLF/null byte validation at client.rs:84-92. However, the type\
    \ still uses raw String rather than axiathon-core's TenantId, so the structural\
    \ fix was not applied \u2014 only runtime validation was added. Partial catch."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer marked 'Workspace dependencies properly declared, no direct version
    pinning in crate Cargo.toml' as VERIFIED. However, the workspace Cargo.toml added
    6 deps (clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, reqwest, toml) with direct version
    strings rather than using workspace = true in the crate's Cargo.toml. The Code
    Changes Summary shows Cargo.toml changes but the finding about direct version
    strings vs workspace = true was not flagged.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'RawConfig lacks #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\
    \ \u2014 typos silently accepted' and separately flagged [MEDIUM]: 'Config silently\
    \ discards token/api_key with no warning \u2014 an operator putting a token in\
    \ cli.toml gets zero feedback that it's being ignored.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [LOW]: 'siem_client_constructs_with_base_url test\
    \ has vacuous assertion \u2014 siem_client_test.rs:20: assert!(client.is_ok()\
    \ || true, ...) \u2014 the || true makes this assert always pass'. Also flagged\
    \ config_test.rs:79-82 vacuous assertion."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged config_test.rs:79-82 as [LOW]: 'assert!(result.is_ok()\
    \ || result.is_err(), ...) \u2014 a Result is always either Ok or Err. This assertion\
    \ can never fail.' This is the zero-assertion/vacuous test issue. The specific\
    \ 'let _ = config' pattern with no assertions was caught indirectly through the\
    \ vacuous assertion findings."
